---
/*
 * Evidence, not screenshots.
 *
 * Two proofs of deliberately different kinds: a clip of hardware doing the
 * thing, and the literal output of a classifier reading hostile traffic. The
 * previous version stacked two identical showcase boxes, which gave the eye no
 * reason to rank them. A moving image and a block of text cannot compete.
 */
---

<section id="demo" class="proof-section site-container" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <div class="section-heading reveal-item">
    <p class="eyebrow lang-en">evidence</p>
    <p class="eyebrow lang-es">evidencia</p>
    <h2 id="proof-title">
      <span class="lang-en">Proof, not screenshots.</span>
      <span class="lang-es">Pruebas, no capturas.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>

  <figure class="proof-primary reveal-item">
    <div class="proof-frame">
      {/* preload="none" on purpose: nothing is fetched until someone presses
          play, so a visitor who never watches pays nothing for the file. */}
      <video
        class="proof-video"
        controls
        preload="none"
        playsinline
        muted
        poster="/demos/psychron-poster.jpg"
        width="1280"
        height="720"
      >
        <source src="/demos/psychron-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        <span class="lang-en">Your browser cannot play this video.</span>
        <span class="lang-es">Tu navegador no puede reproducir este vídeo.</span>
      </video>
    </div>

    <figcaption class="proof-caption">
      <div class="proof-rail">
        <span class="proof-id">01 / psychron</span>
        <span>ESP32 · DHT22 · SSD1306</span>
        <span>MQTT · mTLS</span>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Zoel-Manchon/psychron" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          <span class="lang-en">repository</span>
          <span class="lang-es">repositorio</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="lang-en">
        A hand over the sensor and the whole chain moves. Real hardware on a breadboard: the node signs its telemetry with a client certificate and publishes over mutual TLS — humidity climbs on the dashboard as it climbs on the display.
      </p>
      <p class="lang-es">
        Una mano sobre el sensor y la cadena entera se mueve. Hardware real sobre protoboard: el nodo firma su telemetría con un certificado de cliente y publica sobre TLS mutuo — la humedad sube en el panel a la vez que sube en la pantalla.
      </p>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="proof-record reveal-item">
    <div class="proof-rail">
      <span class="proof-id">02 / honeytrap</span>
      <span>MQTT · CoAP</span>
      <span class="lang-en">8 scripted attacks</span>
      <span class="lang-es">8 ataques guionizados</span>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Zoel-Manchon/honeytrap" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        <span class="lang-en">repository</span>
        <span class="lang-es">repositorio</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="proof-output" role="img" aria-label="Honeypot classifier output: four attack scenarios and the verdict each produced">
      <div class="proof-row">
        <span class="proof-scenario">credential_bruteforce</span>
        <b class="proof-verdict">BRUTE_FORCE</b>
        <span class="proof-note">5 distinct credential pairs</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-row">
        <span class="proof-scenario">wildcard_harvest</span>
        <b class="proof-verdict">WILDCARD_HARVEST</b>
        <span class="proof-note">subscription to full wildcard</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-row">
        <span class="proof-scenario">coap_amplification</span>
        <b class="proof-verdict is-hot">AMPLIFICATION_ATTEMPT</b>
        <span class="proof-note">5 replies suppressed</span>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-row">
        <span class="proof-scenario">coap_open_proxy</span>
        <b class="proof-verdict is-hot">OPEN_PROXY_ABUSE</b>
        <span class="proof-note">proxy option in CoAP request</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="proof-record-note lang-en">
      Verbatim classifier output. The verdict belongs to the session, not the packet — and the two CoAP rows returned <b>zero bytes</b>: answering them would have turned the honeypot into a reflector aimed at a third party.
    </p>
    <p class="proof-record-note lang-es">
      Salida literal del clasificador. El veredicto pertenece a la sesión, no al paquete — y las dos filas CoAP devolvieron <b>cero bytes</b>: responderlas habría convertido el honeypot en un reflector apuntando a un tercero.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo-more reveal-item">
    <p>
      <span class="lang-en">More attack-driven demos live in the repositories:</span>
      <span class="lang-es">Más demos basadas en ataques dentro de los repositorios:</span>
    </p>
    <div>
      <a href="https://github.com/Zoel-Manchon/agrisentinel" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">agrisentinel SOC ↗</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/Zoel-Manchon/aegis-zero-trust" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">aegis attack range ↗</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/Zoel-Manchon/emberwall" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">emberwall live boot ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
